# CI typecheck before every PR push

Web `ci` and `mobile` / `mobile-tests` fail constantly when agents skip local
typecheck. **Do not push / open / update a PR until these are green locally.**

## Required pre-push checks (every frontend-touching change)

From repo root, after editing `apps/web` or `apps/mobile`:

```bash
# Web (matches CI `web` job — uses npm, not pnpm)
cd apps/web && npm install && npm run typecheck

# Mobile (matches CI `mobile` + `mobile-tests` typecheck step — uses pnpm)
cd apps/mobile && pnpm install && bash scripts/mobile-typecheck.sh
```

If `node_modules` is missing or tsc can't resolve `next` / packages, install
in that app dir first with the same package manager CI uses (web=`npm`,
mobile=`pnpm`). Local stale/missing installs are not an excuse to skip.

## Recurring failure pattern (fix this BEFORE inventing new theory)

```
error TS18047: 'room' is possibly 'null'.
```

Typical cause: optional chaining on `room?.x` then later `room.room_id` without
narrowing. **Always early-return after a null guard**, then use definite fields:

```typescript
// BAD — CI fails: room still possibly null after room?.presenting
const welcome = room?.welcome_message?.trim();
if (!welcome || room?.presenting) return;
spokenRef.current = room.room_id;  // TS18047

// GOOD
if (!room) return;
const welcome = room.welcome_message?.trim();
if (!welcome || room.presenting) return;
spokenRef.current = room.room_id;
```

Same rule for any nullable state (`joinInfo`, `me`, `participant`, `slide`).

## Version bump — required on EVERY PR, no exceptions

Every PR must:
1. Advance the `VERSION` file (strictly greater than the fork-point version)
2. Add a `CHANGELOG.txt` entry that names the new version: `- YYYY-MM-DD - vX.Y.Z - <what changed>`
3. Keep `apps/web/app/lib/version.ts` and `apps/mobile/src/version.ts` in sync

**Run this before committing on any PR:**

```bash
python3 scripts/bump_pr_version.py
```

The script auto-detects the bump level, writes all four files, and prints the
new version. Commit those files alongside your actual changes. A PR that skips
this fails the `version-bump` CI job immediately with:

```
::error::VERSION must be bumped on every PR (traceability).
Fork point (abc1234) is 0.20.2; PR is 0.20.2.
Run: python3 scripts/bump_pr_version.py
```

## Lockfile sync — always update pnpm-lock.yaml after touching package.json

CI runs `pnpm install` with `--frozen-lockfile` (the default in CI environments).
If `pnpm-lock.yaml` doesn't match `package.json` the job fails immediately with:

```
[ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE] Cannot install with "frozen-lockfile" because
pnpm-lock.yaml is not up to date with package.json
  Failure reason:
  specifiers in the lockfile don't match specifiers in package.json:
  - react-native-view-shot (lockfile: 5.1.1, manifest: 4.0.3)
```

**Rule: any time you edit `apps/mobile/package.json`, run this before committing:**

```bash
pnpm --dir apps/mobile install
```

Then stage the updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` alongside the `package.json` change in
the same commit. Never commit a `package.json` version bump without the matching
lockfile update — CI will reject it.

Same applies to `apps/web/package.json` (uses `npm` — run `npm install` in that
directory and stage the updated `package-lock.json`).

## Other known gates (do not ignore)

- **Web CI** runs `npm run typecheck` then `npm run build` in `apps/web`.
- **Mobile CI** runs `bash scripts/mobile-typecheck.sh` (uses
  `tsconfig.typecheck.json`, not a casual `tsc` with wrong cwd).
- **mobile-tests** also runs typecheck first; a TS error fails the job before
  Jest. Fix typecheck — do not treat mobile-tests as “Jest/Babel only.”
- After a full pytest suite, mobile version files may be clobbered — restore
  them before commit (see `run-and-test-locally` skill).

## When CI is already red on a PR

1. `gh pr checks` / `gh run view <id> --log-failed` — read the actual TS errors.
2. Fix the reported lines; re-run the local typecheck commands above.
3. Commit + push; do not open a second PR for the same branch.
